CloudBurrow patch 57 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1555).

The bug: CloudBurrow's front runs queries of its own (reads a check
needs, the change history, the table of INFORMATION_SCHEMA.JOBS rows),
which are no client's jobs, and knew them by job ID in its memory alone,
the last 5,000 of them. After a front restart, or 5,000 of them later,
jobs.list and INFORMATION_SCHEMA.JOBS listed every earlier one as the
client's (measured in the BigQuery compat suite: 1,306 jobs before a front
restart, 3,684 after). The engine makes a jobs.query's job ID itself, so
the front could not choose one it would know again.

The patch reads the header X-Cloudburrow-Job-Id-Prefix (letters, digits,
underscores and dashes, at most 64), which the front sends with its own
queries, and begins the ID of each job it makes for that request with it:
a jobs.query's, and a jobs.insert's that names no jobReference.jobId. A
request without it is unchanged.

